    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster, as his elite 83.29 score reflects an ideal confluence of variables: a friendly park, a favorable platoon split against May, and a projected contribution ceiling that remains unmatched. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier are **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom benefit from pitching matchups that facilitate high-volume offensive output. **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing; his score of 67.58 is bolstered by a slow pitcher delivery that improves our stolen base potential\u2014a critical consideration given our strategic emphasis on speed. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** earns a 64.71 rating, benefiting from an elite SP skill boost and a strong 0.379 xwOBA, proving he is a high-floor asset against Sears.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung**, who landed at a 42.88 score\u2014respectable, but ultimately suppressed by a difficult matchup against Cease. While **Josh Jung** is a viable talent, he failed to crack the top ten due to the superior projected efficiency of **Coby Mayo** and **Brayan Rocchio**, who, despite lower raw tools, find themselves in more favorable park and pitching environments. Meanwhile, we are exercising extreme caution with **Henry Bolte**; his 41.35 score puts him dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold. His matchup against Espino is statistically grim, as the opposing starter\u2019s 1.94 xERA acts as a massive anchor on his production. We are deploying **Henry Bolte** only to ensure we reach necessary game caps, as his upside is severely limited by the elite caliber of the opposing arm. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile nature of these mid-September matchups. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.25) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.29) provide veteran stability, any late-breaking weather patterns or lineup shifts could jeopardize the projected efficiency of the bottom half of our order, specifically **Luis Lara** and **Brayan Rocchio**. With **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL, the depth of our bench is being tested, but the current configuration maximizes our probability of netting positive gains in the categories that matter most. We are prioritizing high-contact, high-speed profiles today to maintain our standing in a competitive Roto field.",
